<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
    <dict>
        <key>Description</key>
        <string>This import is NOT verified yet: the download has no hard check (no vendor hash, no signature check). A real run is refused by the shared importer until a verification step exists, unless the override sets pcman_allow_unverified to true (the run then publishes with a WARNING, and the report says published, NOT verified). Hands the downloaded Foxit PDF Reader installer (an EXE) to the package tool (pcman), which publishes it as a new version of the template item into the Cimian repository, or says that nothing is new. For an EXE the package tool is given the version label: the recipe passes the version that the shared WindowsExeVersion step read from the file itself, which is the ProductVersion that a person reads in the file's properties. On 2026-10-02 it was 2026.2.1.39815, and the version in Foxit's address, 2026.2.1, was its first three parts; that the next release keeps this is NOT established, and whether the package tool checks that an EXE is the same product as the template was NOT established. This is a dry run, which writes nothing, until the recipe's override sets pcman_dry_run to false.</string>
        <key>Identifier</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.cimian.FoxitReader</string>
        <key>Input</key>
        <dict>
            <key>NAME</key>
            <string>FoxitReader</string>
            <key>PCMAN_TEMPLATE</key>
            <string>foxitreader</string>
        </dict>
        <key>MinimumVersion</key>
        <string>1.0.0</string>
        <key>ParentRecipe</key>
        <string>com.github.serrc-techops.download.FoxitReader-Win</string>
        <key>Process</key>
        <array>
            <dict>
                <key>Processor</key>
                <string>com.github.serrc-techops.SharedProcessors/PcmanImporter</string>
                <key>Arguments</key>
                <dict>
                    <key>pathname</key>
                    <string>%pathname%</string>
                    <key>pcman_template</key>
                    <string>%PCMAN_TEMPLATE%</string>
                    <key>pcman_version</key>
                    <string>%version%</string>
                </dict>
            </dict>
        </array>
    </dict>
</plist>
